INT. SEED VAULT - ARCTIC ISLAND - NIGHT

A frozen concrete tunnel, shelves of sealed foil packets disappearing into the dark. Every breath is a cloud.

IVO LUNDQVIST, forties, a thief in a thermal suit, kneels at a steel case, a pry bar in his gloved hands. His earpiece crackles.

NORA (V.O.)
(over earpiece)
Ivo, you have six minutes before the guard rotation.

IVO
(whisper)
I know.

He cracks the case. It opens. Inside lies a single glass vial, pale gold.

NORA (V.O.)
(over earpiece)
Don't touch it. Is it the right strain?

He lifts it to the light. He turns it. He sets it back.

IVO
Wrong label.

NORA (V.O.)
(over earpiece)
Then try the next case.

He rises. He crosses the tunnel in three strides. He pries the second case. A siren starts low and climbs. Ivo lunges backward, slips on the ice, and the vial flies out of his hand.

NORA (V.O.)
(over earpiece)
Ivo! What happened?

Ivo and the vial hang in the air for a long beat. He catches it a hand's width above the floor. The siren stops. Silence.

IVO
Got it.

NORA (V.O.)
(over earpiece, quiet)
Good. Now turn around.

He does. A single red dot rests on his chest. At the end of the tunnel, the guard lowers a rifle.

IVO
Nora?

NORA (V.O.)
(over earpiece)
He pays better.
